  "result": "`test/orders.js` is order-total utilities for a shop backend: `calcTotal` sums item price×qty, `applyDiscount` applies a percent-off code, `averageItemPrice` averages item price, `formatOrder` renders a receipt with line items and discounted total.\n\nBug: `calcTotal` (line 5) uses `i <= items.length`, an off-by-one that reads past the array end (`items[items.length]` is `undefined`), throwing a `TypeError` on `.price`. Should be `i < items.length`. This also breaks `averageItemPrice` and `formatOrder`, which both call `calcTotal`.\n\nSecondary bug: `averageItemPrice` (line 20) divides by `items.length` with no empty-array check, yielding `NaN` for `[]`.",
